title: The Civic bloc comes apart

@ko_collapse
# scenario-ledger: KO-07, KO-08, KO-09, KO-10, KO-13
# prose-audit: Grade A — The break is caused by whichever KO failure the player actually produced, and the scene says which one; the departing wing, its leader and the size of the walkout are fixed before any choice is offered, so Lewica chooses what to do about a rupture rather than whether to cause one.
title: KO stops being able to hold its own people
subtitle: A wing of the Civic bloc leaves; Lewica decides whether the wreckage becomes a partner, a rival or its own recruits
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 30
order: 5
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ko_collapsed = 0 and ko_collapse_pressure >= 68 and ko_seats >= 15 and snap_campaign_active = 0 and sikorski_nightmare = 0 and election_2027_terminal = 0
on-arrival: {!
const koSeats = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0));
const pressure = Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_collapse_pressure) || 0);
// The cause is whichever failure the player actually produced, in the order
// that would be reported: a convention that could not decide, a collapsed
// poll, an unbearable coalition, or a leadership nobody could remove.
Q.ko_collapse_cause = Q.ko_convention_failed
    ? "convention"
    : (Number(Q.ko_poll) || 0) < 19
        ? "polling"
        : (Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) >= 55
            ? "coalition"
            // A party that lost the 2020 runoff claim and never found another
            // one does not break over a succession; it breaks over the years
            // spent arguing about a number.
            : Q.ko_hegemony_broken
                ? "hegemony_2020"
                : "succession";
const taken = function(name) {
    return name == Q.president_name || name == Q.ko_leader ||
        name == Q.prime_minister ||
        (name == "Rafał Trzaskowski" && Q.trzaskowski_joined_left);
};
const pick = function(names) {
    return names.find(function(name) { return !taken(name); }) ||
        "a founding committee";
};
// The wing that lost control of the party is the wing that leaves it.
const progressiveWing =
    (Number(Q.ko_social_liberal_share) || 0) >=
    (Number(Q.ko_classical_liberal_share) || 0);
Q.ko_break_wing = progressiveWing ? "Classical-liberal" : "Progressive";
Q.ko_break_leader = progressiveWing
    ? pick(["Radosław Sikorski", "Adam Szłapka", "Marcin Kierwiński"])
    : pick(["Barbara Nowacka", "Rafał Trzaskowski", "Adam Szłapka"]);
Q.ko_break_size = Math.max(4, Math.min(
    Math.round(koSeats * 0.42),
    Math.round(koSeats * (0.10 + pressure / 320))
));
Q.ko_collapse_stance = "Undecided";
Q.news_headline = "A wing of KO announces it is leaving";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The bloc stops holding

[? if ko_collapse_cause = "convention": KO never settled what it legally is.
The convention that was meant to answer the question produced an adjournment
and a set of boards that have now told their members, in public, that the
other components cannot be trusted with the lists. Everything since has been
conducted between organisations that no longer expect to survive together.?]
[? if ko_collapse_cause = "polling": KO's support has fallen far enough that
its own regional structures can do the arithmetic. At this level a common list
returns fewer mandates than the sum of what its parts believe they could win
apart, and enough people believe it to act on it.?]
[? if ko_collapse_cause = "coalition": The coalition has cost KO more than it
can carry. Every concession made at the government table has been paid for by
the same wing, and that wing has finished paying.?]
[? if ko_collapse_cause = "succession": Nobody could remove **[+ ko_leader
+]** and nobody could work under **[+ ko_leader +]** indefinitely. The
succession that never happened inside the party is now happening outside it.?]
[? if ko_collapse_cause = "hegemony_2020": Every internal argument since June
2020 has been the same argument. **[+ pres_2020_ko_name +]** finished on **[+
ko_2020_r1_share +]%** and KO has spent the years since being a large party
that cannot say why anybody should concentrate behind it. The wings blamed
each other for the number then, and they are still doing it.?]

<span class="party-ko"><b>[+ ko_break_leader +]</b></span> leads the departure. Roughly **[+ ko_break_size +]
MPs** of the [+ ko_break_wing +] wing intend to sit separately, taking their
regional organisers, their donors and their claim to be the part of KO that
was right. What remains keeps the name, the debts and the harder half of the
electorate.

[? if government_party = "ko": The cabinet's arithmetic goes with them. A
government built on KO's caucus does not survive the loss of a wing without
either replacing those votes or explaining to the President why it still
has a majority.?]

Lewica cannot stop this and did not have to cause it. It can decide what the
break is for.

- @ko_collapse_shelter
- @ko_collapse_prop
- @ko_collapse_ground
- @ko_collapse_finish

@ko_collapse_shelter
title: Offer the departing progressives places with us
subtitle: A third of the leavers join Lewica outright and the rest found a friendly party; the rump treats us as the reason it broke.
view-if: ko_break_wing = "Progressive"
on-arrival: ko_collapse_stance = "Shelter the departing wing"; progressive_credibility += 4; local_network += 3; ko_relation -= 8; news_headline = "Lewica offers KO's departing progressives a home"

We put list places, staff and committee positions in writing before anyone
else does. The people who spent the last two years losing internal votes on
housing, schools and rights are offered somewhere those votes are won. Some
take it and sit with us; the rest found their own party and remember who
opened the door. KO's remaining leadership tells every journalist that the
Left dismembered its coalition partner, and will keep saying it.

- @ko_collapse_result: Read the settlement

@ko_collapse_prop
title: Hold the rump together
subtitle: Cuts the walkout by nearly half and keeps the democratic bloc's arithmetic alive; we gain nothing and defend a party we spend the rest of the term arguing with.
on-arrival: ko_collapse_stance = "Hold the rump together"; ko_relation += 9; progressive_credibility -= 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica works to keep KO's remainder standing"

We spend our credibility on somebody else's party: joint statements, shared
platforms, a guarantee that the coalition's programme survives the fight.
Several MPs who had signed the departure decide that leaving now means being
blamed for whatever follows, and stay. The democratic majority keeps its
numbers. Our own members watch the leadership rescue a liberal party and ask
what precisely we received for it.

- @ko_collapse_result: Read the settlement

@ko_collapse_ground
title: Take the ground rather than the MPs
subtitle: No mandates change hands; we campaign in the space KO is vacating and let it break at full size.
on-arrival: ko_collapse_stance = "Take the ground"; local_network += 3; media_capacity += 2; party_system_left_pull += 3; left_poll += 0.4; ko_relation -= 3; news_headline = "Lewica campaigns into the space KO is vacating"

We do not bid for a single mandate. Our organisers go instead to the towns
where KO's structure has just stopped functioning: the councillors with no
regional office to call, the voters with nobody canvassing them. Nothing
changes in the Sejm arithmetic this month. In eighteen months there is a Left
presence where there used to be a Civic one, which is the slower and larger
prize.

- @ko_collapse_result: Read the settlement

@ko_collapse_finish
title: Make the break public and final
subtitle: Widens the walkout by a quarter and destroys the pretence of a common bloc; the right inherits part of what breaks.
on-arrival: ko_collapse_stance = "Finish it in public"; ko_relation -= 14; media_capacity += 3; konf_poll += 0.4; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica declares the Civic bloc finished"

We say what everybody in the building knows: the party that ran the government
no longer exists as one thing, and its commitments were signed by an
organisation that has stopped meeting. The rupture goes from a wing's decision
to a public fact, and more MPs move than intended to. Some of them do not move
toward us. A quarter of KO's disillusioned voters were never going to look
left, and Konfederacja is waiting for exactly this.

- @ko_collapse_result: Read the settlement

@ko_collapse_result
title: The Civic bloc splits
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const group = function(id) {
    return (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
        return record.id == id;
    });
};
const koSeats = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0));
const stance = Q.ko_collapse_stance;
const stanceScale = stance == "Hold the rump together"
    ? 0.55
    : stance == "Finish it in public" ? 1.25 : 1;
const leavers = Math.max(1, Math.min(
    koSeats - 1,
    Math.round((Number(Q.ko_break_size) || 4) * stanceScale)
));
const toLewica = stance == "Shelter the departing wing"
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(leavers / 3))
    : 0;
const splinterSeats = Math.max(0, leavers - toLewica);
Q.ko_seats = koSeats - leavers;
Q.ko_splinter_active = 1;
Q.ko_splinter_type = Q.ko_break_wing;
const iplSplinter = Q.ko_break_wing == "Progressive" &&
    Q.ko_break_leader == "Barbara Nowacka";
// The classical-liberal wing does not sit as a nameless caucus. It re-founds
// Platforma Obywatelska outside the Civic bloc under a new registration:
// Nowa Platforma, with the old party's regional barons, donors and claim to
// the succession, and a badge that is deliberately not KO's.
Q.ko_splinter_name = iplSplinter
    ? "Inicjatywa Polska"
    : Q.ko_break_wing == "Classical-liberal"
        ? "Nowa Platforma"
        : Q.ko_break_wing + " KO splinter";
Q.ko_splinter_class = iplSplinter
    ? "party-inicjatywa-polska"
    : Q.ko_break_wing == "Classical-liberal"
        ? "party-np"
        : "party-ko";
if (iplSplinter) Q.snap_progressive_ko_candidate = "Monika Rosa";
Q.ko_splinter_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_splinter_seats) || 0) + splinterSeats;
Q.ko_collapse_defectors = toLewica;
if (toLewica > 0) {
    Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + toLewica;
    Q.left_progressives_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) + toLewica;
    Q.left_new_generation_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_new_generation_seats) || 0) + toLewica;
    Q.nowa_lewica_seats =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.nowa_lewica_seats) || 0) + toLewica;
}
// A collapsing party goes to whoever holds the apparatus, unless Lewica
// spent its credibility keeping the incumbent upright.
const taken = function(name) {
    return name == Q.president_name || name == Q.ko_break_leader ||
        (name == "Rafał Trzaskowski" && Q.trzaskowski_joined_left);
};
const rumpLeader = ["Marcin Kierwiński", "Barbara Nowacka",
    "Radosław Sikorski", "Rafał Trzaskowski"].find(function(name) {
        return !taken(name);
    }) || "a collective presidium";
Q.ko_leader_previous = Q.ko_leader;
Q.ko_leader = stance == "Hold the rump together" &&
    (Number(Q.ko_poll) || 0) >= 20 && !taken(Q.ko_leader)
    ? Q.ko_leader
    : rumpLeader;
Q.ko_leader_changed = Q.ko_leader != Q.ko_leader_previous ? 1 : 0;
Q.ko_collapsed = 1;
Q.ko_collapse_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.ko_collapse_settlement_time = (Number(Q.time) || 0) + 4;
Q.ko_collapse_shock = 0;
Q.ko_convention_failed = 0;
Q.ko_cohesion = stance == "Hold the rump together" ? 52 : 42;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.round((Number(Q.ko_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.5)
);
Q.ko_poll = Math.max(4, (Number(Q.ko_poll) || 20) - 1.2);
Q.ko_collapse_result = Q.ko_break_wing +
    " wing leaves with " + splinterSeats + " MPs" +
    (toLewica > 0 ? " and " + toLewica + " cross to Lewica" : "");
const genericSplinter = group("ko_splinter");
if (genericSplinter) genericSplinter.active = iplSplinter ? 0 : 1;
const splinter = group(iplSplinter ? "ipl" : "ko_splinter");
if (splinter) {
    splinter.active = 1;
    splinter.name = Q.ko_splinter_name;
    splinter.leader = Q.ko_break_leader;
    splinter.bloc = "ko";
    splinter.kind = "party";
    splinter.parent = "Civic coalition";
    splinter.allied = 0;
    splinter.legal_status = Q.ko_break_wing == "Classical-liberal"
        ? "registered party re-founding Platforma Obywatelska"
        : "independent organisation";
    splinter.list_committee = "ko_splinter";
    splinter.club = "ko_splinter";
    splinter.independent = 1;
    splinter.organisation = 30 + Math.min(20, splinterSeats);
    splinter.cohesion = 62;
    splinter.mp_count = splinterSeats;
    splinter.sejm_mps = splinterSeats;
    splinter.exclusive_seats = splinterSeats;
}
const koParty = group("ko_party");
if (koParty) {
    koParty.cohesion = Q.ko_cohesion;
    koParty.mp_count = Q.ko_seats;
    koParty.sejm_mps = Q.ko_seats;
    koParty.leader = Q.ko_leader;
}
// A cabinet resting on KO's caucus loses those votes on the day they leave.
Q.ko_collapse_government_shock = 0;
if (
    Q.government_party == "ko" &&
    Q.government_has_confidence && !Q.caretaker_government
) {
    Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_support_seats) || 0) - leavers
    );
    Q.government_coalition_dissent =
        (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) + 8;
    Q.early_election_risk = Math.max(
        Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0,
        stance == "Hold the rump together" ? 40 : 62
    );
    Q.ko_collapse_government_shock = 1;
}
Q.news_headline = "KO splits: " + Q.ko_collapse_result;
!}

= [+ ko_collapse_result +]

**[+ ko_break_leader +]** registers **[+ ko_splinter_name +]** with **[+
ko_splinter_seats +] MPs**; **[+ ko_leader +]** is left with a smaller,
angrier and considerably more governable KO of **[+ ko_seats +]**. Both will
appear on the next ballot, and neither can reach the other's voters without
the name they have just finished fighting over.

[? if ko_break_wing = "Classical-liberal": The breakaway does not present itself
as new. Its founding declaration says it is re-founding Platforma Obywatelska —
the party the Civic bloc was built on and then, in its telling, spent — under a
registration KO's board cannot touch, with a different colour and a different
badge on the same regional structures. **[+ ko_leader +]** keeps the trademark;
**[+ ko_break_leader +]** claims the inheritance.?]

[? if ko_collapse_defectors > 0: **[+ ko_collapse_defectors +]** of the
departing MPs sit with us rather than with the breakaway. They bring
constituency organisations, not just votes, and they bring a permanent
argument with our own members about who the Left is now for.?]
[? if ko_collapse_stance = "Hold the rump together": Our intervention kept
part of the walkout in place. KO survives as one recognisable party and knows
precisely who paid for that, which is worth something in every negotiation
until it isn't.?]
[? if ko_collapse_stance = "Take the ground": No mandate moved. The
organisational vacuum is ours to fill, on a timescale measured in elections
rather than months.?]
[? if ko_collapse_stance = "Finish it in public": The break is total and
public. Part of the wreckage does not come to us: disillusioned Civic voters
who wanted competence rather than a programme are now available to anybody
promising it louder.?]

[? if ko_leader_changed: KO's leadership passes to **[+ ko_leader +]**;
**[+ ko_leader_previous +]** could not survive presiding over the break.?]
[? if ko_collapse_government_shock: The cabinet has lost those votes. Its
majority now depends on whoever can be assembled from a chamber that has just
watched the largest governing party divide in public.?]

- @ko_collapse_finish_record

@ko_collapse_finish_record
title: Return the split to the leadership table
go-to: poland_event_queue

@ko_splinter_settlement
# prose-audit: Grade A — The breakaway is a live organisation with its own arithmetic rather than a scoreboard entry: it must choose between a list, a pact and irrelevance, and Lewica's three answers each decide something different about whose voters those are at the next election.
title: The breakaway decides what it is for
subtitle: A separate party with no threshold cushion asks Lewica for a list, a pact or nothing
face-image: img/poland/events/donald-tusk-2023.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and ko_collapsed = 1 and ko_splinter_active = 1 and ko_splinter_settled = 0 and time >= ko_collapse_settlement_time and snap_campaign_active = 0 and ko_splinter_seats >= 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.ko_splinter_poll_estimate = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round((Number(Q.ko_splinter_poll) || 0) * 10) / 10
);
Q.news_headline = Q.ko_break_wing +
    " breakaway asks what it stands on at the next election";
!}

= [+ date_label +] — A party with a caucus and no floor

**[+ ko_break_leader +]**'s breakaway has offices, a caucus and roughly **[+
ko_splinter_poll_estimate +]%**. On a separate list that is a party which may
return nobody at all; the 5% threshold does not care how right anybody was.
Its options are somebody else's list, a pact that keeps its identity, or a
campaign it can lose entirely on its own.

[? if ko_break_wing = "Progressive": Its programme overlaps ours on rights,
housing and public services, which makes an offer possible and makes it
expensive: everything we concede to them is a place our own candidates
wanted.?]
[? if ko_break_wing = "Classical-liberal": Its economics are not ours and
never were. What it has is the anti-PiS vote in constituencies where we are
weak, and the ability to take that vote somewhere worse.?]

- @ko_splinter_list
- @ko_splinter_pact
- @ko_splinter_ignore

@ko_splinter_list
title: Put them on our list under our rules
subtitle: Their MPs become Left mandates and their organisation becomes ours; our own candidates lose the places they occupy.
choose-if: ko_break_wing = "Progressive" and left_poll >= 10
unavailable-subtitle: A classical-liberal caucus will not stand on a Left programme, and a Left polling this low cannot shelter anybody.
on-arrival: {!
const joined = Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.ko_splinter_seats) || 0));
const iplSplinter = Q.ko_break_leader == "Barbara Nowacka" &&
    Q.ko_splinter_type == "Progressive";
Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) + joined;
Q.left_progressives_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_progressives_seats) || 0) + joined;
Q.left_new_generation_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_new_generation_seats) || 0) + joined;
Q.nowa_lewica_seats =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.nowa_lewica_seats) || 0) + joined;
Q.ko_splinter_seats = 0;
Q.ko_splinter_active = 0;
Q.ko_splinter_settled = 1;
Q.ko_splinter_outcome = "Joined the Left list with " + joined + " MPs";
if (iplSplinter) {
    Q.ipl_joined_left = 1;
    Q.left_ipl_current_seats = joined;
}
Q.barons_dissent = (Number(Q.barons_dissent) || 0) + 6;
Q.progressives_strength = (Number(Q.progressives_strength) || 0) + 3;
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 2;
Q.left_poll = (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) + 0.5;
const splinter = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == (iplSplinter ? "ipl" : "ko_splinter");
});
if (splinter) {
    splinter.active = 1;
    splinter.bloc = "left";
    splinter.kind = "current";
    splinter.parent = Q.left_party_name || "Lewica";
    splinter.legal_status = "internal civic-progressive current";
    splinter.allied = 1;
    splinter.list_committee = "left";
    splinter.club = "left";
    splinter.independent = 0;
    splinter.exclusive_seats = 0;
}
Q.news_headline = "KO's breakaway joins the Left list";
!}

They stand where we stand, under our programme and our discipline, and their
**[+ ko_splinter_outcome +]** are counted as ours from the day the agreement
is signed. Our regional secretaries are told which winnable places have just
been given away to people who spent a decade opposing us on tax. The Left is
larger and less certain what it is.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the settlement

@ko_splinter_pact
title: Sign a constituency pact and leave them their name
subtitle: Both lists survive; we agree where not to compete and neither of us can claim the other's result.
on-arrival: ko_splinter_settled = 1; ko_splinter_outcome = "Standing alone under an electoral pact"; ko_splinter_pact = 1; public_trust += 2; local_network += 1; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "A constituency pact keeps the breakaway on the ballot"

Neither organisation dissolves. We agree which constituencies each of us works
and which senate seats go uncontested, and we sign it publicly so that neither
side can quietly break it. They keep a chance of clearing the threshold; we
keep a partner who owes us nothing and can leave whenever the arithmetic
changes.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the settlement

@ko_splinter_ignore
title: Let them find out what a threshold is
subtitle: No offer. They rejoin KO, dissolve or fail, and we inherit whatever is left of their voters.
on-arrival: {!
const splinterSeats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_splinter_seats) || 0);
const returning = (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) >= 45;
const iplSplinter = Q.ko_break_leader == "Barbara Nowacka" &&
    Q.ko_splinter_type == "Progressive";
Q.ko_splinter_settled = 1;
if (returning) {
    Q.ko_seats = Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) + splinterSeats;
    Q.ko_splinter_seats = 0;
    Q.ko_splinter_active = 0;
    Q.ko_cohesion = Math.min(80, (Number(Q.ko_cohesion) || 42) + 10);
    Q.ko_splinter_outcome = "Returned to KO with " + splinterSeats + " MPs";
    Q.news_headline = "The breakaway returns to KO rather than face a threshold";
    if (iplSplinter) Q.snap_progressive_ko_candidate = "Barbara Nowacka";
} else {
    Q.ko_splinter_outcome = "Standing alone with no agreement";
    Q.left_poll = (Number(Q.left_poll) || 0) + 0.2;
    Q.news_headline = "The breakaway will contest the election alone";
}
const splinter = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == (iplSplinter ? "ipl" : "ko_splinter");
});
if (splinter && returning) {
    splinter.active = iplSplinter ? 1 : 0;
    splinter.bloc = "ko";
    splinter.kind = Q.ko_consolidated ? "current" : "party";
    splinter.parent = "Koalicja Obywatelska";
    splinter.allied = 1;
    splinter.legal_status = Q.ko_consolidated
        ? "internal KO current"
        : "allied party";
    splinter.list_committee = "ko";
    splinter.club = "ko";
    splinter.independent = 0;
    splinter.mp_count = iplSplinter ? splinterSeats : 0;
    splinter.sejm_mps = iplSplinter ? splinterSeats : 0;
    splinter.exclusive_seats = 0;
}
!}

We make no offer and answer no letters.

[? if ko_splinter_outcome = "Standing alone with no agreement": They announce
a separate list, which is the announcement of a party that has decided to find
out how much of KO's vote was ever theirs. Whatever they fail to convert is
available to whoever is still organising in those towns.?]
[? if not ko_splinter_outcome = "Standing alone with no agreement": Faced with
a threshold and no partner, the caucus negotiates its way back into KO on
worse terms than it left. The rupture is repaired as a defeat rather than a
reunion, and everybody who watched it happen has learned what leaving costs.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Record the settlement

@ko_after_collapse_channels
# prose-audit: Grade A — The April 2026 channel question survives KO's collapse instead of assuming it away: with the bloc split there is no single doorway to buy, only a rump that needs cover and a breakaway that needs a floor, and choosing one costs the other.
title: Two Civic parties, one coalition seat
subtitle: After the split, Lewica can only maintain one serious relationship on that side of the table
