= April 2026 — Which half

The Civic bloc no longer has a leader who can deliver it, because it is not
one thing to deliver. **[+ ko_leader +]** runs a rump party with the name, the
machine and the debts. **[+ ko_break_leader +]** runs a breakaway with the
better argument and no floor under it. Both need something from us before the
next election and neither can be paid at the other's expense without the other
noticing.

- @ko_after_collapse_rump
- @ko_after_collapse_breakaway
- @ko_after_collapse_neither

@ko_after_collapse_rump
title: Work with the rump party that still has the machine
subtitle: The larger caucus, the state-level negotiations and the discipline; the breakaway concludes we back whoever holds the offices.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Rump KO leadership"; ko_relation += 7; ko_cohesion += 4; progressive_credibility -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica settles its business with what remains of KO"

We deal with the organisation that can still whip a vote. Committee places,
list arithmetic and the coalition's remaining legislative programme are agreed
with people who can deliver them. The breakaway watches a Left party choose an
apparatus over an argument, and files it.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the event desk

@ko_after_collapse_breakaway
title: Build the relationship with the breakaway instead
subtitle: A partner closer to us programmatically and possibly below the threshold; the rump treats every joint appearance as proof we caused the split.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Civic breakaway"; ko_relation -= 6; ko_splinter_relation += 10; progressive_credibility += 3; local_network += 2; news_headline = "Lewica builds its Civic relationship with the breakaway"

We appear with them, legislate with them and treat them as the serious
successor to what KO was supposed to be. It is a bet on a party that may not
clear 5%. If it does clear it, we have a partner whose programme does not need
translating; if it does not, we have spent two years being photographed with
a corpse and the rump remembers every frame.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the event desk

@ko_after_collapse_neither
title: Deal with both and commit to neither
subtitle: Keeps every option open at the price of being nobody's first call when either of them has something to trade.
on-arrival: ko_channel_target = "Both Civic organisations, no commitment"; public_trust += 2; ko_relation += 2; ko_splinter_relation += 3; news_headline = "Lewica keeps both Civic doors open and neither key"

We keep both channels formally open and make no commitment to either. Nothing
is foreclosed, which is genuinely worth something in a chamber this unstable.
It also means that when either party needs a partner in a hurry, it starts the
call somewhere else and reaches us fourth.

- @poland_event_queue: Return to the event desk
